# Test Automation Conventions

## Architecture — four-layer separation, never collapse it

- **`pages/*.page.ts`** — POM classes only. Hold locator references (as `readonly` properties set from locator factory functions) and expose action/query methods. NEVER put raw selector strings directly in a page class — they must come from `utilities/locators/`.
- **`utilities/locators/**/*.locators.ts`** — ALL raw selector strings live here as exported factory functions (e.g. `getSaveButton(page)`). `utilities/locators/index.ts` is a barrel re-export — if a new locator file is added, it must be re-exported there too.
- **`flows/**/*.flow.ts`** — business-logic orchestration. Flow functions instantiate the POM classes they need (page objects are NOT stored in fixtures) and call their methods in sequence. This is where multi-step logic belongs, not in spec files.
- **`tests/**/*.spec.ts`** — THIN wrappers only. A spec file's test body should be a single `await someFlowFunction(page, testInfo)` call, inside a `test.describe` block with a `test.beforeEach` for login/setup.

## Method naming prefixes

| Prefix | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `fill*` | Fill an input/group |
| `click*` | Click an element |
| `ensure*` | Idempotent state guard + action |
| `wait*` / `waitFor*` | Wait for a condition |
| `get*` | Retrieve a value asynchronously |
| `is*` | Boolean state check |
| `collect*` | Scrape and return a data object |
| `verify*` | Post-action assertion, returns boolean |

## Fixtures

- Use `fixtures/test.fixture.ts` (imported via `tests/test.ts`) as the default fixture.
- Only use `fixtures/multi-user.fixture.ts` when a test needs a second storage state.

## Spec file structure

```typescript
import { test } from '../test';
import { LoginPage } from '../../pages/loginPage/login.page';

test.describe('<feature>', () => {
  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    await new LoginPage(page).loginAsExampleUser();
  });

  test('<case name>', async ({ page }, testInfo) => {
    await someFlowFunction(page, testInfo);
  });
});
```

## Naming conventions

| Type | Convention |
|---|---|
| Page objects | `camelCase.page.ts` |
| Spec files | `camelCase.spec.ts` |
| Flow files | `camelCase.flow.ts` |
| Locator files | `camelCase.locators.ts` |
| Helper files | `camelCase.helper.ts` |
| Auth setup | `kebab-case.auth.setup.ts` |
| Fixtures | `kebab-case.fixture.ts` |

## Never touch unless asked

Do not modify `utilities/locatorHeal/`, `utilities/locatorFailure/`, or `scripts/locator-heal/` unless explicitly requested — those belong to the optional self-healing system.
